From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Line-buffer stdout

nuubos-scraper follows the per-game progress lines through a pipe, where
stdout was block-buffered: progress arrived in bursts of several games.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
---
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -136,6 +136,10 @@
 
 
 int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
+    // nuubOS: a pipe gets every line at once (the progress lines
+    // "#n/m, (found/missed)" drive nuubos-scraper's progress), not in 4 KiB
+    // blocks.
+    setvbuf(stdout, NULL, _IOLBF, 0);
 #if defined(Q_OS_LINUX) || defined(Q_OS_MACOS)
     struct sigaction sigIntHandler;
 
